description:
1. BD Director/Senior Manager


**Key Responsibilities:**  
1. Identify and evaluate new business opportunities in the pharmaceutical industry.


2. Build and maintain relationships with key stakeholders including customers, partners, and industry leaders.


3. Work with cross-functional teams to advance projects collaboratively.


4. Conduct market research and analysis to understand industry trends and the competitive environment.


5. Negotiate contracts and agreements with partners.


6. Engage and develop potential partners in the pharmaceutical industry, for out-licensing agreements of both innovative new medicine and established generic drugs.


**Required Abilities:**  
1. Degree/Master in pharmacy, biology or medical related majors;


2. At least 5 years of business development experience in the pharmaceutical industry;


3. Have experience in successfully completing drug out-licensing, technology transfer, mergers and acquisitions and other transactions;


4. Understand the regulatory requirements and compliance standards of the pharmaceutical industry;


5. Have an in-depth understanding of out-licensing transactions, technology transfer and M&A dynamics in the pharmaceutical industry;


6. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills;


7. Strong presentation and public speaking skills.


Kanghong Pharmaceutical Group is listed on the Shenzhen Stock Exchange, was founded in 1996, and engages in R&D, manufacturing, and marketing products in the ophthalmology, central nervous system, cardiovascular, and metabolism fields. Our company focuses on innovative drug pipelines in gene therapy, oncology assets, dementia, and pain management.


We have 599 patents and more than 4800 employees, including our U.S. and Singapore entities. Our Singapore wholly owned subsidiary, Medical ProSearch Hub, is responsible for APAC (excluding China PRC) markets in commercializing our therapeutic drugs & TCM product, as well as exploring partnerships of both out-licensing our innovative drug pipelines and in-licensing.
